/-!
# Descending Koszul-regularity along a closed immersion

Let `Z --i--→ Y --j--→ X` be closed immersions of schemes with ideals `I ⊆ J ⊆ O_X`, and let `x`
run over the image of `Z`.  If `I` and `J` are Koszul-regular and the map of cotangent fibres
`I_x/𝔪_x I_x ⟶ J_x/𝔪_x J_x` is injective, then the ideal of `Z` in `Y` is Koszul-regular.  This
is part (3) of [Stacks Project, Tag 068Z] with the injectivity — the one consequence the source
draws from exactness and local splitness of the conormal sequence — taken as the hypothesis.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf.cotangentFibreMap`: the map `I/𝔪I ⟶ J/𝔪J` of
  cotangent fibres induced by an inclusion of ideals of a local ring.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf.conormalFibreMap`: that map for the defining ideals
  of `j` and of `i ≫ j` at the image of a point of `Z`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf.exists_koszulRegular_sections_of_basis`: part (3)
  of [Stacks Project, Tag 067N], a lift of a basis of the cotangent fibre of a Koszul-regular
  ideal sheaf is a Koszul-regular family of generators near the point.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf.exists_adapted_koszulRegular_sections`: local
  generators of `I` extending to local generators of `J`, both Koszul-regular.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf.isKoszulRegularIdealSheaf_of_comp`: the descent
  itself.

## Implementation notes

A Koszul-regular family of generators of an ideal sheaf is quasi-regular at every point, so its
germs are a basis of the cotangent fibre; the comparison of two such families by an invertible
matrix of sections is `Stacks.RingedSpace.exists_invertible_change_of_local_generators`, and
[Stacks Project, Tag 066A] transfers Koszul-regularity between them germ by germ.  Injectivity on
cotangent fibres lets a basis coming from generators of `I` be completed to a basis coming from
generators of `J`, and the two lifts agree on a smaller open because their germs at `x` agree.

On an affine open the resulting families generate the two kernel ideals and are Koszul-regular
there, so [Stacks Project, Tag 068M] applies to the concatenation: the images of the second family
in the quotient by the ideal of `Y` are Koszul-regular, and that quotient is the ring of sections
of `Y` over the preimage of the affine open.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 068Z](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/068Z)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 068M](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/068M)
